  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARQMO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Quilombolas are Afro-Brazilian forest communities - around 6,000 groups nationwide - whose territories in the Karib region form a vital buffer between heavily deforested ranching areas and major Indigenous and conservation zones. Facing threats such as illegal logging, mining, land grabbing, and destructive infrastructure, they work through their umbrella association ARQMO. Regnskogsf&#xf6;reningen supports ARQMO in combating invasions, strengthening local governance, advancing socio-economic development, empowering women and youth, and promoting sustainable use of natural resources to protect their lands and cultural identity.</narrative>
  </description>
